# Production Deployment Workflow

Dev machine and production PC are **different machines**. Production updates via **git pull** on branch **`deploy/production`** — not USB unless git is unavailable.

## Agent obligation after production-affecting changes

When you change any runtime file (`backend/`, `relay/`, `frontend/`, `extension/`, `start.bat`, `restart.bat`, `setup-production.bat`, `data/macbook_intake.xlsx` template):

1. **Run** `package-for-production.bat` from repo root (non-interactive: `cmd /c "call package-for-production.bat < NUL"`). Confirms `dist\TRC_Opt\` packages cleanly. `dist/` is gitignored — not pushed.
2. **Commit** on branch **`deploy/production`** with a clear message.
3. **Push** to `origin deploy/production`.
4. **Tell the user** to run on the production PC:
   ```bat
   cd C:\TRC_Opt
   git pull origin deploy/production
   ```
   Then reload the Firefox extension and run `start.bat` (or `restart.bat`).

Do **not** push to `main` for production deploys unless the user explicitly asks.

Do **not** tell the user to run `setup-production.bat` on pull unless `relay/package.json` or `backend/requirements.txt` changed.

Do **not** commit or overwrite production Excel data — `data/macbook_intake.xlsx` on production is protected with `git update-index --skip-worktree` (one-time on production).

## Production PC one-time git setup

```bat
git clone https://github.com/appsdothingsiguess/TRCOptimizer.git C:\TRC_Opt
cd C:\TRC_Opt
git checkout deploy/production
setup-production.bat
git update-index --skip-worktree data/macbook_intake.xlsx
```

Load Firefox extension, log in to i3, run `start.bat`. Use **`http://localhost:4321`** only (relay binds `127.0.0.1`).

## Production PC every update

```bat
cd C:\TRC_Opt
git pull origin deploy/production
```

Reload extension in `about:debugging`, then `start.bat`.

## Branch policy

| Branch | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `main` | Development history |
| `deploy/production` | What the TRC production PC pulls |

## Localhost-only (no IT firewall prompts)

- Relay: `127.0.0.1:4321`
- Extension HTTP: `http://127.0.0.1:4321/...` (not `localhost` — Firefox IPv6 mismatch)
- Extension WebSocket: `ws://localhost:4321/ws` (works as-is)
